## DESCRIPTION
## Perform a row operation on a matrix.
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## KEYWORDS('matrix','row operation')

## DBsubject('WeBWorK')
## DBchapter('Linears and Linear Function')
## DBsection('Problem')
## Date('September 5, 2008')
## Author('Peter Staab')
## Institution('Fitchburg State University')

# updated 2023.11.10

DOCUMENT();    # This should be the first executable line in the problem.
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'MatrixReduce.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context("Matrix");

$A = Matrix([ map { [ map { random(-6, 6) } (1 .. 4) ] } (1 .. 3) ]);

$q = non_zero_random(-3, 3);
($row1, $row2) = random_subset(2, 1 .. 3);
$A2 = row_add($A, $row1, $row2, $q);

BEGIN_PGML
Consider the augmented coefficient matrix:

[``` [$A] ```]

Perform the Row Operation [` [$q] R_{[$row2]} + R_{[$row1]} \rightarrow R_{[$row1]} `] on the matrix.

[_]*{$A2}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
In this case, we perform the indicated row operation and note that

[```[$q] R_{[$row2]} = [@ 3* $A->row($row2)@]```]
and adding this to row [$row1] and adding results in 
[```[$q] R_{[$row2]} + R_{[$row1]} = [@ 3* $A->row($row2) + $A->row($row1) @] ```]
and then replacing row [$row1] with this results in the matrix:

[```[$A2]```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();
